  "id": "contiguity",
  "term": "contiguity",
  "definition": "In learning, contiguity means that different stimuli occur close together in time. In classical or Pavlovian conditioning, this temporal closeness can produce a learned response even when the response is not followed by rewarding or unpleasant consequences.",
